28. Subjects with known or suspected history of a clinically significant systemic disease, unstable medical disorders, life-threatening disease or current malignancies that would pose a risk to the subject in the opinion of the Investigator;
29. Participation in another investigational drug clinical trial within 1 month (30 days) or having received an investigational drug within the last month (30 days) before the start of screening;
30. Is judged by the Investigator to be unsuitable for any reason.

Inclusion Criteria:

1. Gastroscopy biopsy confirmed a solitary gastric adenocarcinoma;
2. White light endoscopy, magnifying endoscopy-image-enhanced endoscopy，(ME-IEE）, endoscopic ultrasound and enhanced CT comprehensively assessed as cT1N0M0, with no distant metastasis;
3. Assessed by MDT as unsuitable for simple ESD: including cases beyond the current guideline/consensus recommended ESD curative resection indications, or although at the endoscopic treatment border, significant fibrosis, scarring, non-lifting and other factors make complete endoscopic resection difficult and surgical function-preserving treatment has reasonable benefits;
4. Lesion maximum diameter in principle ≤5 cm; for lesions close to 5 cm, near the cardia/pylorus or expected to cause stenosis or significant gastric deformation after local resection, they are listed as key review cases before surgery, and gastric preservation path can be directly abandoned during surgery;
5. ECOG performance status score 0-1, able to tolerate general anaesthesia and laparoscopic surgery;
6. Patient fully understands the potential benefits and uncertainties of SNNS/LECS, the possible false-negative risk of ICG single tracing and intraoperative pathology, as well as the possibility of conversion/additional standard radical gastrectomy, and has signed the informed consent form.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Preoperative imaging, endoscopy or MDT suggests cT2 or above, definite lymph node metastasis or distant metastasis;
2. Pregnant or breastfeeding women;
3. Previous major upper abdominal surgery leading to expected severe adhesions, significantly affecting SLB localisation or surgical implementation;
4. Recurrent gastric cancer, multiple primary gastric cancers, or those who received preoperative radiotherapy and chemotherapy;
5. Cases that have undergone ESD removal and achieved curative resection according to eCura standards;
6. History of severe ICG allergy or deemed unsuitable by the researcher to use ICG;
7. Patients with other untreated malignant tumours, severe cardiopulmonary dysfunction, or other conditions unable to tolerate general anaesthesia and pneumoperitoneum;
8. Those unable to understand the study process or complete standard follow-up.

