主要终点:
Cumulative Restoration Success Rate via Modified USPHS Criteria

Proportion of restored crowns categorized as clinically successful (expressed as a percentage).

Restoration success is defined as achieving Alpha (A) or Bravo (B) ratings across all four Modified USPHS parameters evaluated via visual, explorer, and dental floss inspection:

1. Marginal Integrity (Alpha = smooth adaptation; Bravo = explorer catches);
2. Color Match (Alpha = exact match; Bravo = acceptable mismatch);
3. Restoration Integrity (Alpha = intact; Bravo = small material loss);
4. Proximal Contact (Alpha = normal resistance to floss; Bravo = contact present without resistance).

A rating of Charlie (C) or Delta (D) in any single parameter constitutes restoration failure.

Evaluated at 3, 6, and 9 months post-operative.

